 "notes": [
  "All transistors are 4-terminal symbols with a separately drawn bulk wire: PMOS bulks wired to the vdd rail (PM4 and PM5 via 'vdd' labels), NMOS bulks to 'vss' labels.",
  "The 'vss' label is rendered in several ways ('VSS','VS6' left of V1, 'V99' right of V3); all read as the same vss net, which is used as ground.",
  "Voltage source polarity read from the rotated +/- marks: V1 + on PM6 gate side, V3 + on NM2/NM1 gate side, V0 and V2 + at top (gate node), - to vss.",
  "PM3 drain node (mir) is tied to the gates of NM3 and NM0 (self-biased cascode mirror): wire from diamond at PM3 drain to the NM3/NM0 gate line.",
  "Crossings without dots read as not connected: the PM4-drain wire (to NM0 drain node) crosses the PM3/NM2 column and the mir wire; the mir wire crosses the NM2/NM1 gate line.",
  "PM5 (gate vin1) drain goes to NM3 drain / NM2 source (fold_l); PM4 (gate vin2) drain goes to NM0 drain / NM1 source (fold_r).",
  "Net names other than vdd, vss, vin1, vin2, vout are assigned by the transcriber.",
